AWK(1)                        User Commands

NAME
    awk - pattern-directed scanning and processing language

SYNOPSIS
    awk [-F fs] [-v var=value] [-safe] [--version] program [file...]
    awk [-F fs] [-v var=value] [-safe] -f program_file [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    Reads the files (or standard input) as records, splits every record
    into fields and runs the program's pattern-action pairs on it. This is
    the One True AWK of Brian Kernighan (the second edition), and
    implements the language of the POSIX standard and of the book The AWK
    Programming Language: BEGIN and END blocks, regular expression and
    relational patterns, ranges, the built-in variables NR NF FS OFS RS ORS
    FILENAME FNR SUBSEP RSTART RLENGTH ENVIRON ARGC ARGV, associative
    arrays with for (k in a), delete and in, user functions, printf,
    getline in its forms, output to files and pipes, close, fflush and
    system, the string functions length substr index split sub gsub match
    sprintf tolower toupper, the arithmetic functions int sqrt exp log sin
    cos atan2 rand srand, and the time functions systime strftime mktime.
    Strings are UTF-8; length and substr count characters.

    -F fs sets the field separator, -v assigns a variable before BEGIN,
    -f reads the program from a file (repeatable), -safe disables file
    output, pipes and system, and --version prints the release.

SEE ALSO
    sed(1), grep(1), sh(1), index(7)
